The interface fonts
-------------------
public/fonts/<family>/, declared in src/styles/fonts.css and served from
the app's own origin. All four are under the SIL Open Font License,
Version 1.1, and are redistributed with it: each folder holds its family's
OFL.txt as the upstream release ships it, copyright line included.

    ibm-plex-sans-arabic/
      IBM Plex Sans Arabic 1.005, from IBM's package @ibm/plex-sans-arabic
      1.1.0 (https://github.com/IBM/plex). Copyright 2017 IBM Corp., with
      Reserved Font Name "Plex". The Regular, Medium and SemiBold woff2
      files exactly as IBM ships them, unmodified, since a modified version
      may not carry the reserved name.

    reem-kufi/
      Reem Kufi 2.000, from the v2.0 release of
      https://github.com/aliftype/reem-kufi. Copyright 2015-2022 The Reem
      Kufi Project Authors, with Reserved Font Name "Josefin Sans" (the
      source of its Latin, which is not shipped). ReemKufi-Arabic.woff2 is
      the variable ReemKufi.ttf subset to Arabic letters, marks, digits and
      punctuation and converted to woff2; it keeps its own name, which is
      not the reserved one.

    amiri/
      Amiri 1.003, from the 1.003 release of
      https://github.com/aliftype/amiri. Copyright 2010-2022 The Amiri
      Project Authors; no Reserved Font Name. Amiri-Regular-Arabic.woff2
      and Amiri-Bold-Arabic.woff2 are Amiri-Regular.ttf and Amiri-Bold.ttf
      subset to Arabic letters, marks, digits and punctuation and converted
      to woff2.

    amiri-quran/
      Amiri Quran 1.003, from the same release and under the same terms.
      AmiriQuran.woff2 is AmiriQuran.ttf converted to woff2 and nothing
      more: it sets the Quran's text when a page font cannot load, so it is
      never subset, and src/styles/fonts.test.ts checks that it draws every
      character of the 604 pages.

Subsets and conversions were made with fontTools, keeping every layout
feature and every name record.


If you bring in a new dataset, font, photograph or audio source, add it here
in the same pass.
